<title>OnChangeLanguage Global Function</title>


<subheader>Format</subheader>

<logicsyntax>
function OnChangeLanguage();
</logicsyntax>


<subheader>Description</subheader>

The <logiccolor>OnChangeLanguage</logiccolor> global function allows you to execute certain code after the user has changed the <link define_languages.csdoc>language</link> via the CSEntry Options menu. This function must be placed in <logiccolor>PROC GLOBAL</logiccolor>.


<subheader>Return Value</subheader>

The return value of the function is ignored.


<subheader>Example</subheader>

<logic>
function OnChangeLanguage()
    setvaluesets(concat("_", getlanguage()));
end;
</logic>


<seealso cspro_program_structure.csdoc user_defined_functions.csdoc />
